WEBVTT

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:11.480
<v Ananya Rao>Thanks for making time, Dev. So just to set context, Verdant Kitchens is our ready-to-cook meal kit brand, we launched in Bangalore eighteen months ago and we're now in four cities.</v>

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:24.300
<v Ananya Rao>The problem we have is that we look like every other meal kit startup. Same green packaging, same stock photos of vegetables. We need a brand identity that actually feels premium and modern, because our price point is higher than the competition and right now nothing justifies it visually.</v>

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:33.150
<v Dev Maheshwari>Understood. So the core objective is repositioning Verdant as a premium brand rather than a convenience brand. Is that fair?</v>

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:41.900
<v Ananya Rao>Exactly. Premium but approachable. We don't want to feel intimidating or cheffy. The idea is real cooking made effortless, not restaurant theatre.</v>

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:55.600
<v Kabir Shah>To add to that, our audience is very specific. It's urban working professionals, twenty eight to forty five, mostly double income households in metros, Bangalore, Mumbai, Delhi NCR and Pune. Household income upwards of eighteen lakhs. They cook two or three times a week, not daily.</v>

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:04.200
<v Dev Maheshwari>Got it, so end customers, direct to consumer. Are we also speaking to any retail or partner audience with this?</v>

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:10.300
<v Ananya Rao>Primarily end customers. Retail comes later, let's not scope that in right now.</v>

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:26.400
<v Dev Maheshwari>Right. So on deliverables, from what I'm hearing we're looking at a full brand identity system, logo, colour, typography, packaging direction, and then comprehensive brand guidelines. Plus a new website. Anything on the social side?</v>

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:38.700
<v Ananya Rao>Yes, social media branding too. We post daily on Instagram and it's a mess right now, every post looks like a different company. So templates, a visual language, the whole thing.</v>

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:48.500
<v Kabir Shah>And the website needs to actually convert. Right now it's a Shopify template. We want something modern and engaging that reflects the new identity.</v>

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:57.300
<v Dev Maheshwari>Understood. So brand identity guidelines, social media branding, and the website. Are we doing any video at this stage, a launch film or explainers?</v>

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:05.100
<v Ananya Rao>Not in this phase. Maybe a brand film later once the identity is locked, but let's keep this phase to identity, guidelines, social and web.</v>

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:15.900
<v Dev Maheshwari>Perfect. On messaging, is there a line or a thought that captures what you want people to feel? Even roughly.</v>

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:24.800
<v Ananya Rao>Something like real food, real cooking, zero effort. That's the essence. Good ingredients, you cook it yourself, it takes fifteen minutes.</v>

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:36.600
<v Dev Maheshwari>I like that. And tonally, where do you want to sit? Formal and refined, warm and human, playful?</v>

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:47.400
<v Ananya Rao>Warm, definitely. Not corporate at all. We want people to feel curious, like they're discovering something. And happy, cooking should feel good, not like a chore.</v>

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:56.200
<v Kabir Shah>Agreed. Warm and a little curious. Not witty or jokey though, we've tried that voice and it undercuts the premium positioning.</v>

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:06.400
<v Dev Maheshwari>Noted. And what's the action we want from someone who lands on the site or sees a post? What do they do next?</v>

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:13.200
<v Ananya Rao>Order your first box. That's it. Everything should push towards trying one box.</v>

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:24.500
<v Dev Maheshwari>Clear. On platforms, this lives on the website and social media primarily. Any broadcast or TV in the plan?</v>

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:31.600
<v Ananya Rao>No TV. Website and social only. Everything in English, Indian English, our audience is fully English-first.</v>

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:43.800
<v Dev Maheshwari>Understood. Now on assets, do you have existing brand guidelines or open files we can work from? Logo source files, anything like that?</v>

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:54.900
<v Kabir Shah>We have the logo open files, the AI files from the original designer. There are no real brand guidelines, that's part of why we're here. I'll share the logo files this week.</v>

00:03:55.400 --> 00:04:06.100
<v Dev Maheshwari>That's helpful, thank you. On timelines, what are we working towards? Is there a launch date driving this?</v>

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:18.300
<v Ananya Rao>We want to go live with the new identity and website before Diwali, so realistically we need everything delivered by the fifteenth of November. That's the hard date.</v>

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:27.500
<v Dev Maheshwari>Fifteenth of November, noted. And who's our main point of contact day to day on your side?</v>

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:37.700
<v Ananya Rao>Kabir will be your SPOC, he's our Head of Marketing, he'll handle all the day to day and approvals on creative.</v>

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:45.400
<v Kabir Shah>Yes, I'm the main contact. You can reach me directly, I'll set up a shared channel.</v>

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:56.600
<v Ananya Rao>And if anything gets stuck or you need a decision fast, escalate to me. I'm the founder, I'll unblock it. Anything budget or scope related comes to me.</v>

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:08.300
<v Dev Maheshwari>Perfect, that's clear. Let me put together a brief from this conversation and share it back for confirmation, then we'll follow with scope and timelines.</v>

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:13.500
<v Ananya Rao>Sounds good. Send it across and we'll review by end of week.</v>
